  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced` and kept `totalCents` and `placedAt` alongside them. All 39 tests pass, and `npm run arch` reports no new dependency violations.\n\nI did it this way because ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event. It requires changes to be additive and renames to go through deprecation. A straight rename would break those deployed consumers.\n\n- **Event:** the new fields carry the same values as the old ones. The old fields are marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`.\n- **Tests:** I updated `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check the new fields as well as the old ones.\n- **Left alone:** I didn't touch the `GET /orders/{id}` response shape. ARCH-8 keeps it backward compatible for web-storefront, and you only asked about the event. The internal `Order.placedAt` field is also unchanged.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new names. Once they have, someone can remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`, and `schemaVersion` can be bumped at that point. I left `schemaVersion` at 3 for now because the change is additive.",
